\b Why Microsoft Created Agent Framework\par
\b0 Before MAF, developers commonly used:\par

\pard{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Semantic Kernel\b0  for enterprise integration and orchestration\par
{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}\b AutoGen\b0  for multi-agent collaboration\par
{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}Various custom frameworks for memory, tools, and workflows\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 This created fragmentation and maintenance challenges.\par
Microsoft built MAF to:\par

\pard{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf6\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Unify agent development\par
{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}Support enterprise deployments\par
{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}Provide observability and governance\par
{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}Support multi-agent systems\par
{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}Enable interoperability through MCP and A2A protocols\par
{\pntext\f6\'B7\tab}Move from prototype to production seamlessly\par

